      "math_academy_id": "e-16643",
      "problem": "Complete the missing values in the truth table below.\n\n| $x_1$ | $x_2$ | $x_1 \\downarrow x_2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $0$ | $\\bbox[3pt,border:solid 1pt]{\\phantom{\\textrm{odd}}}$ |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $\\bbox[3pt,border:solid 1pt]{\\phantom{\\textrm{odd}}}$ |\n| $1$ | $0$ | $\\bbox[3pt,border:solid 1pt]{\\phantom{\\textrm{odd}}}$ |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $\\bbox[3pt,border:solid 1pt]{\\phantom{\\textrm{odd}}}$ |",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that $\\textrm{True}=1$ and $\\textrm{False}=0.$ \n\nAlso, the Peirce arrow $x_1 \\downarrow x_2$ is true if and only if both $x_1$ and $x_2$ are false ($0$).\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Boolean function is the following: \n\n| $x_1$ | $x_2$ | $x_1 \\downarrow x_2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $0$ | $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}1}$ |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}0}$ |\n| $1$ | $0$ | $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}0}$ |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}0}$ |",
